				<r3d:description language="eng">Maastricht University Library Digital Collection is the digital heritage showcase of Maastricht University Library. It provides access to digitized and born-digital materials from the university’s special and heritage collections, including manuscripts, rare books, photographs, and art collections. The platform supports education, research, and public engagement by offering structured metadata, IIIF image viewing, and the use of persistent identifiers and external vocabularies (e.g. VIAF, Getty AAT, Geonames, Wikidata) to improve interoperability.</r3d:description>
